Argo CD in a Nutshell: What, Why & How

Recently completed the "Argo CD Essential Guide for End Users with Practice" on Udemy — here’s a quick KT for anyone exploring GitOps and Kubernetes:

📌 What is Argo CD?
 A declarative, GitOps-based continuous delivery tool for Kubernetes. It ensures your cluster state matches the Git repository — your single source of truth.

📌 Why use Argo CD?
Automates and simplifies Kubernetes deployments
Supports rollback, sync strategies, and health checks
Visual UI + CLI support
Enables safer, auditable, and version-controlled deployments

📌 How does it work?
You define app configurations in Git
Argo CD continuously monitors the repo
Any drift from the desired state? Argo CD syncs it back automatically

If you're into CI/CD, Infrastructure as Code, or just want a cleaner way to manage K8s apps — Argo CD is worth exploring! 🚀
